# Figures

```bash
pnpm add --save-dev @mdsvex/plugin-figures@next
```

```js
import { figures } from '@mdsvex/plugin-figures';

mdsvex({ unwrap_images: true, plugins: [figures()] });
```

`:::figure` puts what is written inside it, an image, a code block, a table or a diagram, in a `<figure>` with the bracket text as its `<figcaption>`. It is the one way to make a figure: a lone image stays an image, unwrapped by [`unwrap_images`](/docs/reference/options#unwrap_images).

````svx
:::figure[Sales by month](id=fig:sales)

![A bar chart of sales by month](./chart.png)

:::
````

The `id` is optional and stays on the `<figure>`, as an id you wrote, so one a heading already has fails the build. With `unwrap_images` an image alone in the figure has no `<p>`. A figure has no number of its own: a numbering plugin gives it one through [plugin data](/docs/plugins/writing/plugin-data), and the caption then starts with "Figure 3", or is "Figure 3" alone when the figure has no caption. An empty figure warns (`empty_figure`). `figures({ css: false })` leaves the stylesheet out, and a `figure` from a [directives module](/docs/guides/directives#declaring-directives) replaces the plugin's component.
